bothNow.text:
Soften our hearts which have been hardened by evil, O most pure Virgin;
assuage our grief, O thou who endured many sorrows at the Cross of thy Son;
and listen unto our petitions,//
in that thou art the good one who speedily hearkeneth unto us.

sedalion.text:
The steps of a man are guided aright by the Lord;
wherefore, O holy Olga, He Who trieth the hearts and reins of man guided thee to the kingdom of heaven.//
Through thy supplications may we also not be deprived thereof.

ode3.irmos:
With Thy mighty arm and powerful word Thou didst create heaven and earth;
and Thy Church, which Thou hast redeemed by Thy blood, is established in Thee, crying out://
There is none holy save Thee, O Lord!

ode9.irmos:
Our race departed from Eden because of our first mother, Eve;
but it hath been recalled by thee who for our sake hast given birth to Christ, the new Adam, in two natures, O pure Virgin.
Adam, our forefather, leapt up in joy, having escaped the ancient curse;
and we, boasting in thee, have come to know God because of thee,//
wherefore we magnify thee.

stichera.text:
O brethren, let us praise our Savior and Lord for His most great benefactions;
for, in that He is the Lover of mankind, He placed the fire of divine love in the heart of our first mother Olga,
and through her revealed the abundantly rich fruits of His sowing in our land:
true leaders to the heavenly kingdom among our princes, wise guides to salvation among our hierarchs,
and pillars of faith and piety among every choir of the venerable.//
And through their supplications He saveth our souls from death.

